{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502161-what-are-typical-punishments-for-non-masquerade-siring-violations-of-th-traditions","id":1502161,"title":"What are typical punishments for non-masquerade & siring violations of th Traditions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-04T15:57:51-08:00","id":1502161,"title":"What are typical punishments for non-masquerade & siring violations of th Traditions?","content":"We all know the penalty for violations of the masquerade and the right to sire are death. What about the other traditions? What is the penalty for domain violations, for example?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T16:08:42-08:00","id":1502164,"title":"","content":"Depends on a mixture of factors. Your social and political status definitely count as does the victims and the attitude of the prince<br /> <br /> Genrally, torture, confiscation of property, black listing or revocation of boons are ones I've seen. I once played a neonate tremere who had a brujah anchille storm into my domain haven and kick the shit out of me. Now because the brujah was the childe of the primogen it didn't technically come back on him. But favours had to be called in, they had to directly bribe me (ghouling rights and a boon from brujah primogen....which was immediately fed up the pyramid) and archilli enjoyed the enmity of the Tremere, the sheriff and the prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-02-2023, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T18:49:42-08:00","id":1502172,"title":"","content":"This is an issue that deserves good brainstorming because it is often relevant in chronicles. It's a real problem because vampires don't have the same aversion to certain punishments like humans would - it is either trivial for them to endure or meaningless. Worse from a PC perspective, punishments that should still be deterrents to vampires - like torture - hold little fear for the players because at the end of the day there is no permanent harm on their character sheet (and if there was, they would bitch endlessly about it). (I've only ever seen players act completely defiant about any possible torture because, of course, we're all Hollywood action hero movie stars when we roleplay - I admit I am not much better.)<br /> <br /> I would break down crimes into the two major categories of misdemeanors and felonies, or minor and major violations or however you want to label them. <br /> <br /> The first category is basically about compensating the owner sufficiently for trespassing and property damage (property of course including things like ghouls or even trusted mortal pawns - wergeld should be a thing for vampires). The fine should be sufficient to allow the victim to recover from the damage plus an additional penalty to discourage things again. The exact fine can be any combination of money, service time (boons), or other commodities as agreed between the victim and the transgressor. The Prince is probably just there to mediate or arbitrate between the two parties. He's not acting as a judge. The goal here shouldn't really be punishment, but compensation (plus extra to indicate &quot;sorry&quot;) and to restore the social peace between the two to prevent further violence.<br /> <br /> The second is when the violation is more major, and therefore the society expects something more to be done because of the egregiousness of the crime (which could be the cause for repeated instances of crimes that would otherwise fall in the first category, when the motive is malicious instead of negligent, the criminal has refused to pay earlier agreed damages, etc.) So at this point, what would vampires (and PCs) actually fear?<br /> <br /> At the lower category would be enforced boons to be owed to the aggrieved party. This might be the criminal owing the victim or Prince a boon, or perhaps the transfer of a boon owed by one vampire to the criminal that is now paid to the victim (although I might allow the person who owed the boon to object to the transfer if they had a valid reason). Ideally such a boon would need to be paid in the short term because you don't want boons gained in this manner to linger - it won't seem like a punishment, and it might encourage the criminal to be a scofflaw and never repay.<br /> <br /> The next category would likely be some stage of the blood bond - starting with one drink, but perhaps two or even three depending on the crime. This is the only thing that I've seen actually be a deterrent to PCs as they fear loss of autonomy over their characters more than anything else. But it is something best negotiated with the players out of character as to what crimes make sense for this punishment. You as the ST want a standard of law that the Players can buy into that they feel is correct for the setting (I won't say &quot;just&quot;).<br /> <br /> The last category would be exile on pain of death - basically giving them some time before a Blood Hunt within the domain is called or takes effect. The Blood Hunt will mean the exile is real as they cannot come back. But everyone knows the Prince won't ask other Princes to extend the Blood Hunt to their own domain. The criminal is given some amount of reasonable time to flee. This might be only one day just to allow them to go somewhere safe, or it could be a longer time - three days, a week, a month so they can set their affairs in order (either to better defend the Masquerade, or allow someone to begin transferring matters like ghouls, retainers, influence, etc.).<br /> <br /> In any case, I think a big component of Kindred law is that if you don't kill the vampire, you want the punishment to be in some form that a &quot;reasonable&quot; Kindred won't seek to kill the Prince over it. They acknowledge the punishment is just and are thankful for the extent it allows them to restore the social peace. The Prince wants to minimize the possibility of making enemies, or at least deflect the enmity towards the aggrieved party and not herself. In these cases, enforced boons and a one step blood bond are best.<br /> <br /> Of course, many vampires are not &quot;reasonable&quot;. When caught and punished, they will blame their victims and the law for the punishment, never themselves for committing the crime. In those cases, the Prince will want to take steps to minimize the criminal's future attempts at revenge. In that case, the Prince will likely lean towards deeper blood bonds (2 or 3 steps) or exile as a preventative means.<br /> <br /> These steps are not exclusive. A higher level punishment will likely combine elements of lower levels as the Prince sees fit.<br /> <br /> That's my current take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T19:09:03-08:00","id":1502173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502161-what-are-typical-punishments-for-non-masquerade-siring-violations-of-th-traditions?p=1502172#post1502172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The last category would be exile on pain of death - basically giving them some time before a Blood Hunt within the domain is called or takes effect. The Blood Hunt will mean the exile is real as they cannot come back. But everyone knows the Prince won't ask other Princes to extend the Blood Hunt to their own domain. The criminal is given some amount of reasonable time to flee. This might be only one day just to allow them to go somewhere safe, or it could be a longer time - three days, a week, a month so they can set their affairs in order (either to better defend the Masquerade, or allow someone to begin transferring matters like ghouls, retainers, influence, etc.).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea of exile as a delayed Blood Hunt and used effectively in one of my stories, a version of &quot;Anabelle's Party&quot; from Succubus Club. At the end of the story Lodin sentenced Drummond to exile and tasked the PC's with escorting him in his last night in Chicago. It gave the story a deep and nostalgic tone that was quite memorable (btw, I reduced Drummond's silly factor and just made him a sad and failed railway nostalgic who used to be powerful but had left behind by modernity)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T19:54:19-08:00","id":1502176,"title":"","content":"In my last game the Prince had a close relationship with the local Tremere Chantry. Vampires who broke the Traditions would be punished in various ways, but one in particular was being forced to provide a point of their own blood to the Tremere chantry. Whether the Tremere can <i>actually</i> do anything or not, the idea that they potentially could be using your blood to do some weird magic ritual on you is enough to make many vampires distinctly uncomfortable. Meanwhile the Tremere in that city ended up in a position of law enforcement, with the Chantry working to keep order in the domain (which had suffered from an Anarch uprising and a recent attempted Sabbat invasion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T13:30:45-08:00","id":1502234,"title":"","content":"I tend to refer back to the Revised Edition <b>Guide to the Camarilla</b> which listed some common (and uncommon) sentences for minor, moderate, and serious offenses. Minor offenses might warrant loss of status or title, or forced servitude to another Kindred over time. Moderate offenses might warrant loss of domain, stripping of debts or boons owed, removal of retainers, or forceful one or two step blood bond to the Prince. Serious offenses might warrant destruction of the vampire or their progeny, exile from the city, or, if they choose to stay, branding and/or forcible donation of their blood to the local Tremere Chantry to ensure good behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27764-hasnamuss","name":"Hasnamuss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27764_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T04:48:34-08:00","id":1502296,"title":"","content":"Like IRL medieval times, crime and punishment would be what the prince could get away with, so the prince would need to measure a response that doesn't upset too many of the wrong people while solidifying the power of him and his allies. In &quot;good&quot; cities, the Prince is the arbiter because most agree with his judgement. If the prince is too harsh, he's attacking his constituents, if the prince is too soft, he's playing favourites. The prince can use his power to curb rivals or strengthen allies or to garner favour, but he should at least try to frame things as &quot;fair&quot;. Obviously, Vampires can't expect fairness the way most of us see it: A neonate doesn't have the umph of an elder and can't expect as much consideration. But there's a certain fairness in &quot;one day I too will be old and influentual and will be able to bend the rules more&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Law</b> is good for determining what is a crime and what isn't, but Having the <u><b>Politics</b></u> knowledge should be good for predicting how harsh punishments should be. Ideally, there will be lots of backroom deals before a public sentencing.<br /> <br /> I feel as a prince it would be best to publicly give perpetrators of minor crimes a choice. Similar to &quot;pay a fine or serve a sentence&quot;.<br /> <br /> Non-death examples of punishments:<br /> give up on territory, give away a business or retainer or a lump sum of capital, become blood bound, get staked for a period of time, go into torpor, lose a limb for a time, gain an annoying responsibility, exile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-06-2023, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T04:24:58-08:00","id":1502687,"title":"","content":"The loss of Reputation is also a sort of &quot;punishment&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course it is not enough to quell the vampiric society thirsty for justice and social order, as this is not immediately visible, but it is one thing to keep in mind, particularly for players. If you have a bad rep as someone who doesn't play ball and that is a dishonest liar, at best you can expect others distancing themselves, at worst you may end up dead, caugh up in another kindred's web of manipulations and blamed as a scape goat. After all, it is just too easy to believe that one well know mischief would be responsible for whatever new crime in town.<br /> <br /> This is something players should take heed, even more than a blood bond or something. If start to get marked by the community, you may find troubles constantly coming at your way, and that's something that I think most players - are STs - dont pay too much attention to","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T20:31:35-08:00","id":1503300,"title":"","content":"In the RPG, the only real sort of punishment would be the inability for a PC to play their character, either Death or torpor or buried in cement. We did, have a Neonate PC that trespassed, and got beat up by a more powerful Neonate PC in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T10:42:54-08:00","id":1503331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502161-what-are-typical-punishments-for-non-masquerade-siring-violations-of-th-traditions#post1502161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We all know the penalty for violations of the masquerade and the right to sire are death. What about the other traditions? What is the penalty for domain violations, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see being removed from a Camarilla-related or Clan-based organisation, operation, estabishment, or an institution as a possible consequence for directly (or openly, or repeatedly) breaking the Tradition of Domain or the Tradition of Accounting, for example.<br /> Taking away some of both responsibilities and duties, and also of course profits and benefits, from a particular troublesome or selfish Kindred could as well be effective and also reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T02:40:23-08:00","id":1503363,"title":"","content":"Good old death for both the sire and the young one<br /> <br /> Most conflicts of vampire society come from the fact that 1) Humans can be dicks 2) Vampires are humans with superpowers and that increases their dickery potential 3) Vampire population has overgrown which makes keeping the masquerade and domains difficult.<br /> <br /> However if the character has enough political clout he might get away with whatever they want. Most would not recognize the children, back in the day &quot;Balthazar&quot; the sheriff of Chicago embraced without Lodin permision and the plot indicated that at best he would lost his position, at worst he would be executed. After all if the prince own personal police does not obey his rules who will?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T10:47:03-08:00","id":1503953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502161-what-are-typical-punishments-for-non-masquerade-siring-violations-of-th-traditions?p=1503363#post1503363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good old death for both the sire and the young one<br /> <br /> Most conflicts of vampire society come from the fact that 1) Humans can be dicks 2) Vampires are humans with superpowers and that increases their dickery potential 3) Vampire population has overgrown which makes keeping the masquerade and domains difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 and 2 are great, but you neglect to mention that vampires need to lie, cheat and steal just to live, which weeds out a lot of nice people. But on the otherhand It also weeds out some of the idiots, and idiots are generally the more aggressive types. <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampire overpopulation is really an idea vampires push because they're greedy and paranoid, not an ecological necessity. Far right groups IRL like to advocate for the idea that the world's problems are due to overpopulation. Just like the real world, the population isn't an issue (to a point, but we're certainly not there) , it's just that we don't like to share. Vampires are territorial creatures, but realistically they could swing for far more generous vampires per capita ratio if they were willing. It's in the interest of strong elders to keep the numbers of neonates down to make them easier to manage, but that just makes it a political rulse, not an ecological one. If anything, vampires would suffer more acutely from underpopulation. They need enough numbers to corrupt and infiltrate critical services and lucrative businesses and do dirty deeds humans are incapable of. Even the best ventrue will have uncomfortable blind spots. <br /> <br /> Also the masquerade is pretty easy to keep because movie magic, AI fakery and fake news are everywhere nowadays. Among a whole bunch of other things I won't get into because it's late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T16:53:42-08:00","id":1504146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502161-what-are-typical-punishments-for-non-masquerade-siring-violations-of-th-traditions?p=1503953#post1503953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 and 2 are great, but you neglect to mention that vampires need to lie, cheat and steal just to live, which weeds out a lot of nice people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I read in some of the books that upon being Embraced there is a definite shift in attitude, sensations, and emotions that makes sure that new Kindred can very well find it very easy to adjust and accept the all the different wonderful,new, and interesting needs, occurances and rules that come with being a Vampire. Having the capability and power to affect and influence events, groups, trends, and organizations also helps to a meaningful and also considerable extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-01T21:10:51-08:00","id":1504175,"title":"","content":"I've used all sorts and seen all sorts. Cutting off Limbs, gouging eyes (these grow back). Sunning (exposing them to a certain amount of sunlight) set the door on a timer. Staking for when a problem needs to go away for a time but exile is out of the question. Blood bonding, and I've seen Vampires get stripped of status. There is also timed Bloodhunt, where the prince told them they had to survive a certain amount of time being Hunted but could not leave the city. Or Exile with responsibility, sending someone to a small town or unimportant city to keep them out of your hair, this is used for failures who can learn, but need to lose access to court.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}